{"name":"Silverware","hex":"#b8b8bf","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"silverware","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Anything manufactured from silver.","Anything with a silvery colour. (Can we add an example for this sense?)"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/silverware"}],"entries":[{"title":"Household silver","blocks":[{"text":"Household silver or silverware includes tableware, cutlery, and other household items made of sterling silver, silver gilt, Britannia silver, or Sheffield plate silver. Silver is sometimes bought in sets or combined to form sets, such as a set of silver candlesticks or a silver tea set."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/Toilet_set_in_original_leather_case_MET_DP137849_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Toilet_set_in_original_leather_case_MET_DP137849_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Household_silver","wikidata":"Q1683099"},{"title":"Tableware","blocks":[{"text":"Tableware items are the dishware and utensils used for setting a table, serving food, and dining. The term includes cutlery, glassware, serving dishes, serving utensils, and other items used for practical as well as decorative purposes. The quality, nature, variety and number of objects varies according to culture, religion, number of diners, cuisine and occasion. For example, Middle Eastern, Indian or Polynesian food culture and cuisine sometimes limits tableware to serving dishes, using bread or leaves as individual plates, and not infrequently without use of cutlery. Special occasions are usually reflected in higher quality tableware."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/72/Dining_table_laid_at_Chatsworth_House.jpg/330px-Dining_table_laid_at_Chatsworth_House.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tableware","wikidata":